WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.540
Five paragraphs.

2
00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.230
Your best effort.

3
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:04.790
You hand in your draft.

4
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:10.280
It comes back with one tiny sticky
note, and not a single mark on the page.

5
00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.780
Somewhere in there, one
paragraph is letting you down.

6
00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:14.990
But which one?

7
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.560
If nobody can correct it for you, how
do you find the weak bit yourself?

8
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.350
In this mission, you'll see what
your teacher may say about a draft,

9
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.000
and what they can't do.

10
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.930
You'll work out what to
fix first when you redraft,

11
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.230
and what can wait.

12
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.400
Run a spellcheck?

13
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.100
Start again from scratch?

14
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.470
You'll find out what really
catches a weak paragraph.

15
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.840
Your mission: work out
how to find the weak bit.
